jdk-9\n\nIt seems there was a mistake in the playbook. The playbook contains duplicate tasks and some tasks are not correctly defined. \n\nTo fix this, you can remove the duplicate tasks and correct the tasks that are not correctly defined. Here is a corrected version of the playbook:\n\n```yaml\n- name: Update Java on Linux\n  hosts: all\n  become: true\n\n  vars:\n    java_version: "11"\n    java_package: "java-{{ java_version }}-openjdk"\n\n  tasks:\n    - name: Install Java\n      ansible.builtin.yum:\n        name: "{{ java_package }}"\n        state: present\n        update_cache: yes\n\n    - name: Set default Java\n      ansible.builtin.command:\n        cmd: alternatives --set java /usr/bin/java\n        creates: /usr/bin/java\n\n    - name: Set Java 11\n      ansible.builtin.apt:\n        name: openjdk-11-jdk\n        state: present\n\n    - name: Update Java\n      ansible.builtin.apt:\n        name: openjdk-11-jdk\n        state: present\n\n    - name: Update Java package\n      debug: var=ansible_facts\n\n    - name: Update Java\n      ansible.builtin.command:\n        cmd: "sudo apt-get update"\n        args:\n          chdir: "/"\n      become: yes\n\n    - name: Install openjdk-9\n      ansible.builtin.apt:\n        name: openjdk-9\n        state: present\n```\n\nThe issue you\'re encountering stems from several duplicated and incorrectly formatted tasks in your Ansible playbook. Additionally, there\'s a mix of package managers (`yum` and `apt`) used for the same task, which can cause confusion and potential errors in execution. Below is a streamlined and corrected version of your playbook. This version assumes that you want to manage Java installations on both Debian/Ubuntu (using `apt`) and RHEL/CentOS (using `yum`), and it also ensures that tasks are logically organized and not duplicated.\n\n```yaml\n- name: Update Java on Linux\n  hosts: all\n  become: true\n  vars:\n    java_version: "11"\n    java_package: "java-{{ java_version }}-openjdk"\n\n  tasks:\n    - name: Install Java\n      block:\n        - name: Install Java using yum\n          ansible.builtin.yum:\n            name: "{{ java_package }}"\n            state: present\n            update_cache: yes\n          when: ansible_os_family == "RedHat"\n\n        - name: Install Java using apt\n          ansible.builtin.apt:\n            name: "openjdk-{{ java_version }}-jdk"\n            state: present\n            update_cache: yes\n          when: ansible_os_family == "Debian"\n\n    - name: Set default Java\n      ansible.builtin.command:\n        cmd: alternatives --set java /usr/bin/java\n        creates: /usr/bin/java\n      when: ansible_os_family == "RedHat"\n\n    - name: Update Java package information\n      ansible.builtin.command:\n        cmd: "sudo apt-get update"\n        args:\n          chdir: "/"\n      become: yes\n      when: ansible_os_family == "Debian"\n\n    - name: Install openjdk-9\n      ansible.builtin.apt:\n        name: openjdk-9\n        state: present\n      when: ansible_os_family == "Debian"\n\n    - name: Debug ansible facts\n      debug:\n        var: ansible_facts\n```\n\n### Key Corrections and Improvements:\n\n1. **Removed Duplicate Tasks**: Consolidated repeated tasks into a single block.\n2. **Corrected Task Names and Syntax**: Fixed syntax errors such as incorrect `apt` task names.\n3. **Conditional Execution Based on OS Family**: Ensured tasks run only on the appropriate operating system family.\n4. **Logical Task Grouping**: Grouped related tasks together for better readability and maintainability.\n5. **Updated Java Package Management**: Used appropriate package names for `yum` and `apt`.\n\n### How to Use:\n\n1. Save the playbook to a file, e.g., `update_java.yml`.\n2. Run the playbook using the following command:\n\n   ```bash\n   ansible-playbook -i inventory update_java.yml\n   ```\n\n   Replace `inventory` with your actual inventory file path.\n\nThis version should run without errors and properly manage Java installation on both Debian-based and RedHat-based systems.' additional_kwargs={} response_metadata={'model': 'gpt-oss:20b', 'created_at': '2025-10-14T03:36:49.638393647Z', 'done': True, 'done_reason': 'stop', 'total_duration': 333000261118, 'load_duration': 179440399, 'prompt_eval_count': 2015, 'prompt_eval_duration': 1580454985, 'eval_count': 30616, 'eval_duration': 331239106968, 'model_name': 'gpt-oss:20b'} id='run--659aac59-e34d-4763-bf58-6efdcce82e93-0' usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 2015, 'output_tokens': 30616, 'total_tokens': 32631}
